# Download location

   http://edwardslab.bmcb.georgetown.edu/~nedwards/dropbox/2sqIE5FRG7/

# Installation
   % tar xzf substructure.tgz
   % cd substructure


# Client setup
   Edit submit.py and change the SubstructureSearch.developer_email
   attribute to an appropriate value.

# Client usage - JSON result goes to standard out.
# Uses substructure.glyomics.org by default

   % ./submit.py example.json

# Local server/daemon setup, uses docker

   Edit server/substructure.cfg as needed to choose the port number and the
   number of concurrent searches.

   % cd server
   % ./substructure start

# Client setup

   Edit submit.py and change the SubstructureSearch.apiurl to an
   appropriate value e.g. 'http://localhost:10980'


# Set httpd_user_script_exec_t

   chcon -t httpd_user_script_exec_t /software/substructure/*



# Return JSON

   JSON document, list of lists. Each item is a pair - GlyGen accession,
   true/false whether the substructure alignment is strict or not.

   See: https://glycomotif.glyomics.org/glycomotif/Substructure_Alignment
   for information on strict vs non-strict substructure alignments.

   Cheers!



